Goal: build an embedded ML lock system
Platform/devices:
    XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense (onboard microphone)
    Seeed expansion board (OLED and Sensor Connection).
    Grove infrared sensor
    SD card

ToDos:
  • Read a 4-digit unlock code from a file on the SD card at startup.
  • Display the word LOCK on the OLED while the system is locked.
  • Allow the user to enter the 4-digit code using the IR sensor and mini-controller.
  • If the 4-digit code is correct, generate a random integer from 1 to 7.
  • map that int it to the Password Vocabulary list, and prompt for the password
      - do not tell the user the password, just display the number on the OLED
  • Run an embedded ML inference pipeline on microphone input to recognize the password word.
  • Unlock only when both authentication stages are correct

Design:
    Assumes the SD card has a .txt with "CODE:1234"
    User must speak clearly into the microphone
    Added a reset feature by pressing the button: red-middle-double-arrow 
    The correct color prints to the serial monitor, but the LED will only display it's index

Sources:
    IR remote & buzzer - https://github.com/Arduino-IRremote/Arduino-IRremote?tab=readme-ov-file#examples-for-this-library
                       - https://github.com/Arduino-IRremote/Arduino-IRremote/blob/master/examples/ReceiveDump/PinDefinitionsAndMore.h
    LED - https://github.com/olikraus/u8g2/wiki/u8x8setupcpp#ssd1306-128x64_noname-1
    ML training - https://www.edgeimpulse.com/
    Audio files for colors - https://figshare.com/s/50807c77f1acc943e4c3?file=50448711
    Microphone - TestContinuous (Dr. Blake)

To run:
    Connect XIAO ESP32-S3 to USB
    Open VS Code
    Via pioarduino -> Upload
    Activate Serial Monitor
    Begin entering the PW via remote
